{
    "_note": "Recurring-series programming for Science & Engineering (see channels/publish.php, phase 4). This channel's airtime is now the 12-hour, 12-show repeating lineup added on 2026-11-04 (below): twelve shows, each a real YouTube import with (almost all) candidates approved, each given one fixed 60-minute daily slot plus a second slot exactly 12 hours later -- so the same ordered lineup plays twice every calendar day, i.e. repeats every 12 hours, wall-to-wall with no gaps. A handful of individual episodes (anything longer than the 60-minute slot) were deliberately left unapproved so publish.php never hits its overlap-refusal case; see series/<id>/series.json for exactly which ones. The original phase-4 placeholder blocks ('technology-hour' at daily 13:00, 'engineering-weekly' at Saturday 10:00, for technology-connections/practical-engineering) were removed from here rather than left dormant: because the 12-show lineup below is wall-to-wall across all 24 hours, there is no free airtime left for them to occupy without an overlap -- and each now has exactly one approved episode (from the admin-UI demo commit), so they're no longer actually dormant. technology-connections and practical-engineering remain in catalog.json's series list; they simply have no programming block right now. Re-add a block for either (on a schedule that doesn't collide with the lineup) if they should air again. Phase 10 update (2026-11-05): every block now opts into multi-episode packing (packing.enabled, mode sequential, on_unfit defer, minimum_remaining 30s) so a one-hour slot plays as many complete episodes from each shows real catalog (many of which run well under an hour -- several of these channels mixed in YouTube Shorts) as actually fit, instead of exactly one; any truly-unfilled remainder is handed to the new continuity card (see continuity.json) instead of dead air. boundary.mode is explicitly hard on every block (matching this lineups pre-existing, already-correct behavior): across the whole approved catalog the longest single episode is 3597s, under the 3600s slot, so no block has ever actually needed to run over -- a soft/elastic boundary was evaluated but has nothing real to demonstrate here without inventing an overrun that does not exist in this catalog.",
